  <title>1.11.3: Reasoning Symbolically and Abstractly about Linear Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00244</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.11.3: Reasoning Symbolically and Abstractly about Linear Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4a21ca3e-11e7-4b29-b12e-40fb195885ba</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">For numbers 1 – 5, select the slope and intercept that corresponds to each equation:</para>
      <exercise id="_6c21e788-9cde-4e5b-94cc-e15e1e947b3f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">\( -4x+3y=3 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00004">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00005">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00006">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00007">\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00008">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00009">Correct! \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00010">Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_290e6cf0-44ff-4e9c-88f4-1105c2b6945d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00011">\( 12x-4y=8 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00013">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00014">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00015">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00016">\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00017">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00018">Correct! \( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00019">Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="dc16004d-1b6c-4990-830a-3a35112e31e5" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00020">\( 8x+2y=16 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00022">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00023">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00024">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00025">\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00026">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00027">Correct! \( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00028">Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_85f7342e-2dc9-4623-b35e-32e5737b516d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00029">\( -x+\frac 13 y=\frac 13 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00030">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00031">\( m=3, y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00032">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00033">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00034">\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00035">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00036">Correct! ( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00037">Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_4f72d334-bc7f-4d5d-bf3e-1696a83110e9" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00038">\( -4x + 3y = -6 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00039">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00040">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00041">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,1) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00042">\( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00043">\( m=-4 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,8) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00044">\( m=3 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00045">Correct! \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
          <para id="para-00046">Nice try! The correct answer is \( m=\frac 43 \), \( y\text{-int}=(0,-2) \)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Using Standard Form and Intercepts to Graph</title>
      <para id="para-00047">Standard form, \(Ax + By = C\), is helpful for finding the \(x\)-intercepts and \(y\)-intercepts of an equation.</para>
      <para id="para-00048">For questions 6 - 11,</para>
      <para id="para-00049">
        <quote id="quote-00001">Use the equation \(6x -4y=24\).</quote>
     </para>
      <exercise id="d693b658-f7c3-4288-9f1b-0baf9a491166" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00050">What is the value of \(y\) at the \(x\)-intercept?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00051">Correct! 0</para>
          <para id="para-00052">Nice try! The correct answer is 0.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_8bab532e-ecf3-48f9-a6e5-4505f13ce64e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00053">What is the \(x\)-intercept of the equation?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00054">Correct! 4</para>
          <para id="para-00055">Nice try! The correct answer is 4.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_04605dc6-d8fc-45b1-a167-4208032018fe" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00056">What is the value of \(x\) at the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00057">Correct! 0</para>
          <para id="para-00058">Nice try! The correct answer is 0.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_59849d8c-16fa-497f-85ed-a7fc1d68615a" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00059">What is the \(y\)-intercept of the equation?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00060">Correct! -6</para>
          <para id="para-00061">Nice try! The correct answer is -6.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
