    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Are you ready for more?</title>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
        <para id="para-00068">For numbers 1-2, use the equations below:</para>
        <para id="para-00069">
          <quote id="quote-00002">These are the equations from the activity. Each equation is in the form \(Ax+By=C\)</quote>
       </para>
        <para id="para-00070">\( 4x - 3y = -3 \) \( 12x - 4y = 8 \) \( 8x + 2y = 16 \) \( 3x - y = -1\) \( 4x - 3y = 6 \)</para>
        <exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00003">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            <para id="para-00071">Observe the graph of the equation \(−4x+3y=3\) where it is graphed, on the same coordinate plane, with another line passing through \((0,0)\) and \((A,B)\). In this example \(A=-4\) and \(B=3\), so the other line would pass through \((0,0)\) and \((−4,3)\). What do you notice about the lines?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            <para id="para-00072">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00073">Answers may vary, but here is a sample. The two lines are perpendicular.</para>
            <para id="para-00074">
              
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
